From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: server: the shell's SYSTEM desktop process's token gives what it creates the machine's DACL

David (2026-11-15): Windows Chrome had no sound. Chrome's audio service
(sandboxed, USER_LIMITED) could not open HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT
(ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE), so CoCreateInstance(MMDeviceEnumerator) failed with
REGDB_E_READREGDB. On his machine HKLM\Software\Classes had the descriptor
O:DU D:(A;;GA;;;SY)(A;;GA;;;DU): writable by every user, and readable by no
sandbox, since a restricted token keeps Domain Users only for deny.

The shell's desktop process on the SYSTEM account (an elevated program's
display) takes Wine's admin token (ProcessWineGrantAdminToken), whose
default DACL was upstream's Local System and Domain Users full. The first
key it reached through COM was \Registry\Machine\Software\Classes. combase
creates that key to open it, and SYSTEM stamps a descriptor on a key loaded
from system.reg that has none, so the key got this one. On a shared prefix
that token now has the machine's default DACL, as every other token there
does: SYSTEM and Administrators full; Domain Users, Users, RESTRICTED and
ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES read.

Gate: test/comrestrict-gate.sh (make test-comrestrict), on a shared prefix
with a standard user: a USER_LIMITED low-integrity child reads HKCR and
makes MMDeviceEnumerator before and after a SYSTEM process with the admin
token uses COM, and HKLM\Software\Classes gives Domain Users no more than
read. Mutant SG_MUTANT_ADMIN_TOKEN_UPSTREAM_DACL fails it.
diff --git a/server/token.c b/server/token.c
index 03c5edb..75abdbf 100644
--- a/server/token.c
+++ b/server/token.c
@@ -1434,7 +1434,19 @@ struct token *token_create_admin( unsigned primary, int impersonation_level, int
     /* on Windows, this value changes every time the user logs on */
     struct sid logon_sid = { SID_REVISION, 3, SECURITY_NT_AUTHORITY, { SECURITY_LOGON_IDS_RID, 0, 0 /* FIXME: should be randomly generated when tokens are inherited by new processes */ }};
     const struct sid *user_sid = security_unix_uid_to_sid( getuid() );
+    /* Stained Glass OS: on a shared prefix the machine's default DACL, as every other token there
+     * has (sg_create_system_dacl), not upstream's "Local System and Domain Users full". The shell's
+     * desktop process on the SYSTEM account (an elevated program's display) takes this token
+     * (ProcessWineGrantAdminToken), and the first key it opened through COM -- combase creates
+     * \Registry\Machine\Software\Classes to get at it -- was stamped with that descriptor:
+     * HKLM\Software\Classes writable by every user, and readable by no sandbox, whose token keeps
+     * Domain Users only for deny. Chrome's audio service could not open HKCR, CoCreateInstance
+     * (MMDeviceEnumerator) failed, no sound for any Chrome (David 2026-11-15). */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_ADMIN_TOKEN_UPSTREAM_DACL
+    struct acl *default_dacl = sg_system_prefix ? sg_create_system_dacl( user_sid ) : create_default_dacl( &domain_users_sid );
+#else
     struct acl *default_dacl = create_default_dacl( &domain_users_sid );
+#endif
     const struct luid_attr admin_privs[] =
     {
         { SeChangeNotifyPrivilege, SE_PRIVILEGE_ENABLED },
